          "text": "\n\nExcellent! The implementation is complete and working correctly. Let me write a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `CustomOutput` rendering functionality as specified. Here's what was done:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File: `/workspace/ravenpy/config/commands.py`**\n\nModified the `CustomOutput` class (line 166) to include a custom `to_rv()` method that:\n1. Formats the output as a single line starting with a colon\n2. Uses the command name `CustomOutput` followed by exactly 9 spaces (using format `:{name:<21}`)\n3. Includes the field values (`time_per`, `stat`, `variable`, `space_agg`, and optionally `filename`) separated by single spaces\n4. Excludes empty field values (like the default empty `filename`)\n5. Produces the exact output: `:CustomOutput         YEARLY AVERAGE PRECIP ENTIRE_WATERSHED`\n\n### Key Implementation Details\n\nThe `to_rv()` method:\n```python\ndef to_rv(self):\n    args = []\n    for field in self.model_fields.keys():\n        val = getattr(self, field)\n        if val:  # Only include non-empty values\n            args.append(str(val))\n    \n    return f\":{self.__class__.__name__:<21}\" + \" \".join(args) + \"\\n\"\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n- The command name is formatted with width 21 (producing 9 spaces after `:CustomOutput`)\n- Only non-empty field values are included\n- Fields are separated by single spaces\n- The output ends with a newline\n\n### Verification\n\nThe implementation meets all requirements:\n- ✅ `CustomOutput` can be created with fields `time_per`, `stat`, `variable`, and `space_agg`\n- ✅ Works in model configurations inheriting from `RV` class\n- ✅ Output starts with a colon\n- ✅ Command name and arguments separated by fixed whitespace (9 spaces)\n- ✅ Produces exactly `:CustomOutput         YEARLY AVERAGE PRECIP ENTIRE_WATERSHED`\n- ✅ No additional characters, different spacing, or missing colon\n- ✅ Exposed through public API via `ravenpy.config.commands.CustomOutput`\n- ✅ Can be used in sequence fields with the alias `CustomOutput`",
